<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kittery, Maine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kittery is a town in southern Maine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piscataqua-river">Piscataqua River</a> opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portsmouth-new-hampshire">Portsmouth, New Hampshire</a>. Settled in the 1620s and incorporated in 1647, it is the oldest incorporated town in Maine. It became a centre of shipbuilding, and the Portsmouth Naval Shipyard stands on islands within its bounds.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kittery-maine.jpg" alt="Kittery, Maine" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Greencan7 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lady_Pepperrell_House_Kittery_Point_Maine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
